Interactive Playground Logic (nuqs)
1. URL-State Synchronization
useQueryState: Use useQueryState from nuqs to synchronize component variants (e.g., size, color, boolean toggles) with the browser URL.

Shareability: Every modification in a Pattern Lab playground MUST update the URL parameters so that states are bookmarkable and shareable.

2. Type Safety
Parsers: Use strictly typed parsers (parseAsInteger, parseAsBoolean, parseAsStringLiteral) to ensure URL parameters map correctly to component props.

Defaults: Always provide a defaultValue that matches the component’s default visual state.

3. Performance
Shallow Updates: Use shallow routing by default to prevent unnecessary server-side re-renders during variant toggling.
